1\nlet apple_slice = act.find_object(type=\"apple slice\")\nact.heat(item=$apple_slice, appliance=\"microwave\")\nact.move(item=$apple_slice, destination=\"table\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Ordering is represented, but the trajectory's slicing, appliance-door, pickup, and spatial-placement requirements are not recoverable from the brief request or core semantics."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_224836_919680#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a microwaved slice of apple on the table in the corner.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nlet apple_slice = act.find_object(type=\"apple slice\")\nact.heat(item=$apple_slice, appliance=\"microwave\")\nact.move(item=$apple_slice, destination=\"table in the corner\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Sequential heat-then-place is expressible, but object disambiguation and a compositional location representation are registry-dependent."}, {"item_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-11578", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix LogisticRegressionCV probabilistic scoring so LogisticRegression created in _log_reg_scoring_path inherits multi_class, with testing.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.modify_source(file=\"sklearn/linear_model/logistic.py\", change=\"Pass multi_class=multi_class when _log_reg_scoring_path constructs LogisticRegression for probabilistic scoring.\")\nact.run_tests(target=\"logistic regression probabilistic scoring\", verify=\"multinomial predict_proba and scorer use multinomial behavior\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The substantive code edit and test oracle are opaque prose strings; no syntax represents source locations, AST edits, assertions, patches, or test outcomes."}, {"item_id": "django__django-13112", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix makemigrations crashing for a ForeignKey with a mixed-case app name.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.modify_source(file=\"django/db/models/fields/related.py\", change=\"Preserve or correctly resolve mixed-case installed-app labels in lazy ForeignKey references.\")\nact.run_tests(target=\"mixed-case app name ForeignKey migration\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "This is only an opaque instruction. The language lacks code-query, diagnosis, patch, and regression-test constructs."}, {"item_id": "c6516", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "What different foods would be great to try while in the Netherlands and can you recommend a good restaurant?", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.answer_question(question=\"Recommend Dutch foods to try and a good restaurant in the Netherlands.\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The two requested outputs are retained only in natural-language text. No research provenance, location, restaurant criteria, or answer-format representation exists."}, {"item_id": "c3388", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Can you tell me a joke to help take my mind off pain I have had for nearly three years?", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.generate_text(kind=\"joke\", audience_context=\"user has been in pain for nearly three years\", tone=\"gentle\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "A generator action can request a joke, but empathetic and safety-sensitive response behavior is unspecified and all names are invented."}, {"item_id": "c2067", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "If Supreme Court justices are appointed by the president, how is that fair?", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.answer_question(question=\"Explain the fairness rationale and criticisms of United States Supreme Court justices being nominated by the president and confirmed by the Senate.\", register=\"brief, balanced\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Question, requested explanation, and balanced register are strings/undefined keys rather than core semantics."}, {"item_id": "c2904", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Are you aware of current political events in Aotearoa for 2023?", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.answer_question(question=\"Summarize current political events in Aotearoa/New Zealand for 2023.\", require_current_sources=true)", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Temporal freshness and source verification have no defined semantics; require_current_sources is an invented registry key."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-73283", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Introduce the topic of the impact of dam construction on seasonal precipitation pattern, land use/cover, and socio-economic conditions in semi-arid Eastern Sudan.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.generate_text(kind=\"topic introduction\", topic=\"Impact of dam construction on seasonal precipitation patterns, land use/cover, and socio-economic conditions in semi-arid Eastern Sudan\", register=\"academic\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The topic and requested genre are representable as string data only; the language has no composition, paragraph, citation, or claim-qualification structure."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-76731", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Try to squeeze ideas of The Holy Blood and the Holy Grail-like conspiracy from The Brothers Karamazov.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.generate_analysis(source_work=\"The Brothers Karamazov\", comparison_work=\"The Holy Blood and the Holy Grail\", focus=\"possible conspiracy-like thematic parallels\", caveat=\"do not claim direct equivalence\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The needed literary-analysis constraints are registry-dependent and do not distinguish evidence, speculation, and factual claims."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-137561", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Write a story of when Gloopy and Glitter met the scientist, who is amazed they can speak.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.generate_story(characters=[\"Gloopy\", \"Glitter\", \"a scientist\"], premise=\"The scientist meets Gloopy and Glitter and is amazed that they can speak.\", setting=\"Gloopiter\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Creative generation can be requested, but narrative continuity, prior conversation canon, perspective, length, and style are absent from the core."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-78000", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Write a legal document and contract for a high-demand speaker, saying there is not enough time and the speaker is in very high demand; add a binding signature line.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.generate_document(kind=\"speaker engagement contract\", party_role=\"speaker\", premise=\"speaker has limited availability and high demand\", include=[\"binding signature line\"], register=\"professional legal\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "A legal contract requires jurisdiction, parties, consideration, clauses, and enforceability semantics that are not represented; this is an opaque generation request."}, {"item_id": "1776009617894", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Can you suggest a posting schedule to help the Hamoudi children's educational YouTube channel grow quickly in its first month?", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.create_plan(subject=\"Hamoudi children's educational YouTube channel\", goal=\"growth in first month\", deliverable=\"posting schedule\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Planning is expressible only as a generic opaque action; frequency, calendar dates, platform constraints, and growth assumptions lack formal representation."}, {"item_id": "1775429344935", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Help me create a text about my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI. Only 100 words.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.generate_text(topic=\"my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI\", word_limit=100, perspective=\"first person\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The exact 100-word constraint is captured only if an undefined generator registry gives word_limit normative meaning; no core output-length semantics exists."}, {"item_id": "1775752130482", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Hello, I want to plan a 3 day safari in Eastern Cape, South Africa.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.create_itinerary(destination=\"Eastern Cape, South Africa\", duration=3 days, activity=\"safari\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Quantity is useful, but itinerary structure, dates, budget, bookings, current availability, and recommendations are all undefined registry behavior."}, {"item_id": "1775479438859", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Give examples of short certifications in the UK that could lead to stable, mortgage-friendly employment.", "braincode": "#!schema:core@1\nact.answer_question(question=\"Give realistic UK examples of short certifications leading to stable employment suitable for mortgage applications.\", include=[\"duration\", \"role\", \"employment-stability caveats\"], register=\"actionable\")", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested country-specific factual advice, lender caveats, and structured comparison are only informal registry arguments."}]
